// Project: heating and cooling management for medical office buildings. Type: schematic plan, before and as designed.
// Idea, ORNL/TM-2026/4854 abstract: "The BEMS replaces the standalone thermostats on 11 single-stage heat-pump rooftop
// units, adds circuit-level power metering, and is configured rather than hard-coded for each building."
// Labels and sources (TM-4854):
//   Before, 11 standalone thermostats    abstract (above); 2.2: "standalone, hardwired programmable zone-sensor thermostats"
//   walking to each of the 11 in turn    2.2: "requires a person to walk to each of the 11 thermostats in turn"
//   As designed                          3: "the system as designed for the selected small commercial building"
//   one on-site laptop                   3.1: "Computer (on-site laptop). A single ... laptop hosts the developed software
//                                         and serves as the centralized controller"
//   dashed links                         3.2: "The thermostats and power meters join this device network over Wi-Fi"
//   remote access, cellular router       3.2: "a cellular Wi-Fi router"; "Remote access from off site ends there"
//   5 power meters                       abstract: "11 thermostats, 5 power meters"
//   validated in the laboratory          abstract: "was validated in the laboratory"
// Schematic, not the clinic: a generic 6 + 5 zone rectangle (Table 1: one rooftop unit and thermostat per zone, 11 in all);
// the thermostat and laptop positions and the walking route are illustrative. No coverage circles, no real footprint,
// no real equipment positions.
// Fine-line drawing (classes .dgf in global.css), in the 300 x 356 frame shared by the four project drawings.
// Motion (projects.py in research/compare-2026-10-30-theme-drawings/tools; transform and opacity only, generated
// <style> below): slow by hand versus instant from one place. Intro, once in view: Before draws, then As designed,
// then the links grow out of the laptop, then remote access and the meters. Loop, 9 s: in Before a walker takes the
// route past all 11 thermostats at walking pace, lighting each in turn; in As designed, at the same moment, one pulse
// from the laptop reaches all 11 at once (and again halfway), and data leaves once through remote access.
// Static without JS or with reduced motion.
---
